    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0316" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.3421/45: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-13T14:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 4.50
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Embassy’s January 8, 2 p.m. Da Gama<anchor n="15" xml:id="d268-f1"/> informs me
                    that Brazilian law would support a proposition from an Anglo-American group
                    covering matters contained in Vickers Armstrong proposal forwarded in Embassy’s
                    despatch number 1324 of July 22nd, 1918. Government would prefer joint
                    participation rather than a monopoly by a single nation. This matter should be
                    given immediate attention to prevent Vickers Armstrong from pushing their
                    proposal through.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d268-f1" n="15" xml:id="d268-f1-content">
                <p>Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
